IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`
IMPORT `snap3-s2016a`

-- TESTS for section 2016a (snap3-s2016a.l4). Every expected value is worked out from the text and written beside the assertion, BEFORE running.

§ `Tests -- the dates and the constant`

#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(1) the date from which the 60 days for submitting the plan are counted` EQUALS Date 29 12 2022
-- 29 December 2022 plus 60 days: 2 days to 31 December, 31 more to 31 January, 27 more to 27 February 2023
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(1) the last day for submitting the plan` EQUALS Date 27 2 2023
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2)(C) the first day of the period of theft covered` EQUALS Date 1 10 2022
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2)(C) the last day of the period of theft covered` EQUALS Date 20 12 2024
#ASSERT `s 2016a(a)(3) the last day for promulgating the regulations` EQUALS Date 1 12 2023
#ASSERT `s 2016a(a)(5) the last day for submitting the report` EQUALS Date 1 12 2024
#ASSERT `s 2016a(e)(1) the date from which the year for the Comptroller General's report is counted` EQUALS Date 26 9 2024
#ASSERT `s 2016a(e)(1) the last day for the Comptroller General's report` EQUALS Date 26 9 2025
#ASSERT `s 2016a(d) the amount of the unobligated balances rescinded, in dollars` EQUALS 8000000

§ `Tests -- s 2016a(a) guidance and reports`

#ASSERT `s 2016a(a)(3) the Secretary promulgated the regulations in time` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2016a(a)(3) the Secretary promulgated the regulations in time` (JUST (Date 1 12 2023)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(a)(3) the Secretary promulgated the regulations in time` (JUST (Date 2 12 2023)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(a)(4) the Secretary has done what the paragraph requires` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(a)(4) the Secretary has done what the paragraph requires` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2016a(a)(5) the Secretary submitted the report in time` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2016a(a)(5) the Secretary submitted the report in time` (JUST (Date 1 12 2024)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(a)(5) the Secretary submitted the report in time` (JUST (Date 2 12 2024)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- contents: items (A) to (E)
#ASSERT `s 2016a(a)(5) the report includes what the paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(a)(5) the report includes what the paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(a)(5) the report includes what the paragraph requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement of stolen benefits`

-- arguments: benefit, household, State agency (each from section 2012), the State agency's determination of theft, the date stolen, the amount stolen, the monthly allotment just before the theft, replacements already made in the fiscal year
-- stolen 500, two months of a 300 allotment is 600: the lesser, 500
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement of the stolen benefits` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (Date 15 3 2023) 500 300 0 EQUALS `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement is required up to an amount` 500
-- stolen 800: two months of the allotment, 600, is the lesser
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement of the stolen benefits` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (Date 15 3 2023) 800 300 0 EQUALS `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement is required up to an amount` 600
-- stolen 600 equals two months of the allotment
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement of the stolen benefits` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (Date 15 3 2023) 600 300 0 EQUALS `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement is required up to an amount` 600
-- one earlier replacement in the fiscal year: a second is still within "not more than 2 times"
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement of the stolen benefits` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (Date 15 3 2023) 500 300 1 EQUALS `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement is required up to an amount` 500
-- two earlier replacements: a third is barred
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement of the stolen benefits` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (Date 15 3 2023) 500 300 2 EQUALS `s 2016a(b)(2) the text says no replacement under this section`
-- the period of theft: both ends count
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement of the stolen benefits` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (Date 30 9 2022) 500 300 0 EQUALS `s 2016a(b)(2) the text says no replacement under this section`
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement of the stolen benefits` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 10 2022) 500 300 0 EQUALS `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement is required up to an amount` 500
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement of the stolen benefits` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (Date 20 12 2024) 500 300 0 EQUALS `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement is required up to an amount` 500
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement of the stolen benefits` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (Date 21 12 2024) 500 300 0 EQUALS `s 2016a(b)(2) the text says no replacement under this section`
-- no allotment just before the theft: two months of nothing is nothing
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement of the stolen benefits` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (Date 15 3 2023) 500 0 0 EQUALS `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement is required up to an amount` 0
-- the State agency's determination is its own: not made, or made the other way, the text does not say
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement of the stolen benefits` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (Date 15 3 2023) 500 300 0 EQUALS `s 2016a(b)(2) the text does not say`
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement of the stolen benefits` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (Date 15 3 2023) 500 300 0 EQUALS `s 2016a(b)(2) the text does not say`
-- the section 2012 answers are not all "yes": the text does not say (and this wins over the date and the count)
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement of the stolen benefits` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (Date 15 3 2023) 500 300 0 EQUALS `s 2016a(b)(2) the text does not say`
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement of the stolen benefits` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (Date 15 3 2023) 500 300 0 EQUALS `s 2016a(b)(2) the text does not say`
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement of the stolen benefits` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 1 2020) 500 300 5 EQUALS `s 2016a(b)(2) the text does not say`
-- the date and the count both bar it
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement of the stolen benefits` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 1 2020) 500 300 5 EQUALS `s 2016a(b)(2) the text says no replacement under this section`

§ `Tests -- s 2016a(b) conditions, one at a time`

#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2)(B) another replacement may occur in the Federal fiscal year` 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2)(B) another replacement may occur in the Federal fiscal year` 1 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2)(B) another replacement may occur in the Federal fiscal year` 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2)(B) another replacement may occur in the Federal fiscal year` 3 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2)(C) the stolen benefits fall within the period` (Date 30 9 2022) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2)(C) the stolen benefits fall within the period` (Date 1 10 2022) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2)(C) the stolen benefits fall within the period` (Date 20 12 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2)(C) the stolen benefits fall within the period` (Date 21 12 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1): the plan is submitted by 27 February 2023
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(1) the State agency submitted the plan in time` (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(1) the State agency submitted the plan in time` (Date 27 2 2023) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(1) the State agency submitted the plan in time` (Date 28 2 2023) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1)(A): the six items
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(1)(A) the plan includes what the subparagraph requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(1)(A) the plan includes what the subparagraph requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(1)(A) the plan includes what the subparagraph requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(1)(B) the plan includes what the subparagraph requires` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(1)(B) the plan includes what the subparagraph requires` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(1)(B) the plan includes what the subparagraph requires` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1)(C): arguments are the plan has been approved, the plan has been incorporated
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(1)(C) the plan has been incorporated as the subparagraph requires` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(1)(C) the plan has been incorporated as the subparagraph requires` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(1)(C) the plan has been incorporated as the subparagraph requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1)(D): "may approve after the date": the day of the guidance itself is not after it
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(1)(D) the Secretary may approve the plan` (Date 2 1 2023) (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(1)(D) the Secretary may approve the plan` (Date 1 1 2023) (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(1)(D) the Secretary may approve the plan` (Date 31 12 2022) (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): arguments are the plan was approved, the date asked, the effective date of the rule under (a)(3)
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(3) the plan remains in effect` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(3) the plan remains in effect` TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(3) the plan remains in effect` TRUE (Date 30 6 2026) (JUST (Date 1 7 2026)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(3) the plan remains in effect` TRUE (Date 1 7 2026) (JUST (Date 1 7 2026)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(3) the plan remains in effect` TRUE (Date 2 7 2026) (JUST (Date 1 7 2026)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(4) the replacement is regarded as a loss for the purpose of section 2016(e)` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(4) the replacement is regarded as a loss for the purpose of section 2016(e)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 2016a(c) to (e)`

#ASSERT `s 2016a(c) the terms used in this section have the meaning given in section 2012` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(c) the terms used in this section have the meaning given in section 2012` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2016a(c) the terms used in this section have the meaning given in section 2012` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(d) the unobligated balances remaining after the rescission` 10000000 EQUALS JUST 2000000
#ASSERT `s 2016a(d) the unobligated balances remaining after the rescission` 8000000 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 2016a(d) the unobligated balances remaining after the rescission` 7999999 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2016a(e)(1) the Comptroller General submitted the report in time` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2016a(e)(1) the Comptroller General submitted the report in time` (JUST (Date 26 9 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(e)(1) the Comptroller General submitted the report in time` (JUST (Date 27 9 2025)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): items (A), (B), (C), (D)(i), (D)(ii)
#ASSERT `s 2016a(e)(2) the report includes what the paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(e)(2) the report includes what the paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2016a(e)(2) the report includes what the paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- every constructor declared in snap3-s2016a.l4 is built once`

#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2) the text says no replacement under this section` EQUALS `s 2016a(b)(2) the text says no replacement under this section`
#ASSERT `s 2016a(b)(2) the text does not say` EQUALS `s 2016a(b)(2) the text does not say`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 2016a(b)(2) the text says no replacement under this section` EQUALS `s 2016a(b)(2) the text does not say`)
#ASSERT (`s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement is required up to an amount` 7)'s `the most the replacement may be, in dollars` EQUALS 7
